{
  "vulnerability_found": true,
  "vulnerable_component": "The 'early_done' signal generated by the comparator that checks if the remaining dividend is zero, causing the divider to terminate early and resulting in variable latency dependent on the operand values.",
  "recommended_fix": "Remove the early_done condition and force the divider to always run for a fixed number of cycles equal to the data width. Specifically, eliminate the comparator that generates early_done and modify the control logic so that the done signal is asserted only after the iteration counter reaches the full width, ensuring constant-time execution regardless of the input operands."
